---
import "../sternzeit/sternzeit.css";
import Try from "../Try.astro";
import "./dunstkreis.css";
import "./harmonics.css";

// The nine real spherical harmonics in ENU, band by band, m from -l to l: their polynomials, and what each says of a sky.
const BANDS = [
    { kept: "100%", functions: [{ poly: "1", word: "average", title: "The same everywhere: the sky's average" }] },
    {
        kept: "67%",
        functions: [
            { poly: "y", word: "north", title: "Brighter to the north than to the south, or the other way round" },
            { poly: "z", word: "up", title: "Brighter above than below, or the other way round" },
            { poly: "x", word: "east", title: "Brighter to the east than to the west, or the other way round" },
        ],
    },
    {
        kept: "25%",
        functions: [
            { poly: "xy", word: "diagonal", title: "Northeast and southwest against northwest and southeast" },
            { poly: "yz", word: "tilt north", title: "North high and south low against north low and south high" },
            { poly: "3z²−1", word: "poles", title: "Zenith and nadir against the horizon all round" },
            { poly: "xz", word: "tilt east", title: "East high and west low against east low and west high" },
            { poly: "x²−y²", word: "axes", title: "East and west against north and south" },
        ],
    },
];
const BUILD = [
    { name: "band 0", title: "The average alone: the same light from every side" },
    { name: "bands 0, 1", title: "The average and the three directions" },
    { name: "bands 0 to 2", title: "All nine coefficients, as createIrradiancePass computes them" },
    {
        name: "whole sky",
        title: "The cube map itself, every direction weighted by the cosine: what the nine approximate",
    },
];
---

<figure class="scene-frame" id="harmonics">
    <div class="harmonics-panel" data-variant="both">
        {
            import.meta.env.DEV && (
                <p class="harmonics-variants">
                    <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-variant="both" aria-pressed="true">both</button>
                    <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-variant="a" aria-pressed="false">variant A</button>
                    <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-variant="b" aria-pressed="false">variant B</button>
                </p>
            )
        }
        <div class="harmonics-pyramid">
            <svg class="harmonics-key" aria-hidden="true"></svg>
            {
                BANDS.map((band, l) => (
                    <div class="harmonics-band" data-band={l}>
                        <p class="harmonics-band-name">
                            <span>band {l}</span>
                            <span class="harmonics-kept" title="The share of this band a diffuse surface receives">
                                {band.kept}
                            </span>
                        </p>
                        {band.functions.map((f, m) => (
                            <div class="harmonics-cell" style={`grid-column: ${4 - l + m}`} title={f.title}>
                                <canvas class="harmonics-basis" data-index={l * l + m} aria-hidden="true" />
                                <svg class="harmonics-bars" data-index={l * l + m} aria-hidden="true" />
                                <span class="harmonics-word">{f.word}</span>
                                <span class="harmonics-poly">{f.poly}</span>
                            </div>
                        ))}
                    </div>
                ))
            }
            <p class="harmonics-higher">
                <span>bands 3 to 6</span> <span class="harmonics-kept">0%, 4%, 0%, 2%</span>
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="harmonics-build">
            {
                BUILD.map((step, i) => (
                    <div class="harmonics-step" title={step.title}>
                        <div class="as-seen harmonics-sphere">
                            <canvas data-step={i} aria-hidden="true" />
                        </div>
                        <span class="harmonics-word">{step.name}</span>
                        <span class="harmonics-poly" data-error={i} />
                    </div>
                ))
            }
        </div>
        <svg class="harmonics-plot" aria-hidden="true"></svg>
    </div>
    <label class="figure-slider" data-offset title="The moment, up to half a day either way from where it was set: drag, or turn the mouse wheel for ten minutes a notch">
        <span class="note">Time</span>
        <span class="figure-slider-rail">
            <input type="range" data-field="offset" min="-720" max="720" step="5" value="0" aria-label="Minutes from the moment" />
            <span class="figure-slider-scale" aria-hidden="true">{["−12", "0", "+12"].map((mark, i) => <span class="figure-slider-mark" style={`left: ${i * 50}%`}>{mark}{i !== 1 && <span class="figure-slider-unit">{"\u202fh"}</span>}</span>)}</span>
        </span>
        <output data-field="offsetValue" />
    </label>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        The nine spherical harmonics and the sky held in them. (a) The basis, band by band, each function as its classic
        lobes, reaching as far in every direction as its magnitude there: the accent where it is positive, orange where it
        is negative. Like overtones over a fundamental, each band turns faster around the sphere than the one before;
        beside it, the share of it a diffuse surface receives, nothing at all of band 3. Under each, the sky's coefficient
        in red, green and blue, all to one scale. (b) The sky's irradiance as one such shape, reaching as far in every
        direction as the light on a surface facing it, in its color: from the first band, a sphere, the first two, and all
        three, next to the whole sky's from the cube map, with the horizon at the farthest reach for scale and the Sun's
        direction on it, and how far each is off at worst. (c) The same along the vertical circle through the Sun, from the zenith down to the nadir
        and up again. Drag to rotate.
        <Try label="Evening" set="date=2026-04-06T17:30:00Z&lat=52.395&lon=13.085&h=1" fig="harmonics">
            The shape leans west towards the Sun, and the coefficient of up is positive: the sky outshines the ground.
        </Try>
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./harmonics";
</script>
